leted":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in:\nv4.6.1.stable.official [14d19694e]\nv4.7.dev1.official [bf95b6258]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.1.stable - Windows 11 (build 26100) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - GeForce GTX 550 Ti - Intel(R) Core(TM) i3-2100 CPU @ 3.10GHz (4 threads) - 11.95 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nThe script editor loses focus when the find and replace bar is closed with `esc`, when the Replace or Replace All buttons are focused.\n\nWorkarounds:\nBefore the issue occurs:\n- remember to `shift + tab` to the replace input box before pressing `esc`\n\n After the issue has occurred:\n- mouse click on the script editor to be able to continue typing\n- restore focus from the keyboard with:\n- `ctrl + F1` switch to the 2d view\n- `ctrl + F3` switch to the script editor\n\nWhere the issue doesn't occur:\nThe script editor becomes focused when the find or replace input boxes are focused and `esc` is pressed.\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- open the project: issue-script-editor-loses-focus-on-esc.zip\n- open `test.gd`\n- press: `ctrl + f`\n- type: `abc`\n- press: `ctrl + r`\n- press: `tab` to focus the button: Replace\n- press: `esc`\n- the find and replace bar closes, \n- issue, the script editor isn't focused.\n\nExpected:\nFocus the script editor when the find and replace bar is closed with `esc`.\nThis already happens when the find or replace input boxes are focused and `esc` is pressed.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[issue-script-editor-loses-focus-on-esc.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/25696831/issue-script-editor-loses-focus-on-esc.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://git